# The build dependencies do not include cargo and rustc. The build
# environment installs a pinned Rust toolchain into /usr/opt. The default
# features of ostrya-cli compile liblzma and PCRE2 from their vendored
# sources and link them statically, so the build needs a C compiler from
# build-essential and no -dev package.
Source: ostrya
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Alexey Naidyonov <alexey.naidyonov@gmail.com>
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/growler/ostrya

Package: ostrya
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: gnupg
Description: OSTree repository tool in pure Rust
 ostrya is a pure-Rust, async reimplementation of the ostree repository
 library. It writes the ostree on-disk format byte for byte.
 .
 This package contains the ostrya command-line tool. It initializes,
 commits to, checks out, pulls into, and serves ostree repositories.
